Removes the defect class rather than its symptoms. Codex findings 13 and 14
forced this: 13 was a bug I INTRODUCED in 6972809 (dragFallbackTabIds recorded
fallbacks for panes the preview never touched), and 14 was "you fixed the route
on cancel but not on the same-pane commit" - the identical shape as 11. Ten of
fourteen findings traced to one cause and I was producing them as fast as I
closed them.

What changed my mind about doing this autonomously, having twice declined: the
live preview was MY addition in this PR. The strips used a drop indicator
before it, and the user never asked for a preview - they asked for clicking to
work and for trailing-space append to survive. So this is reverting an
unrequested change of mine that was generating defects, which is the
conservative action, not the bold one. Scope discipline cuts toward removing
it.

Design now: a drag records only { paneId, index } in dropPreview and draws an
indicator. panes is untouched until drop. Everything that reads panes mid-drag
- handleProjectMutation, persistWorkspace, the route sync - now sees the real
workspace, so findings 5-14 are structurally impossible rather than patched.

Deleted: dragSnapshot, origin, the cancel restore, dragFallbackTabIds,
dropDragFallbacks, empty-pane repair on cancel, persist-on-cancel, route resync
on cancel, and the dragover state mutation. Net -285 lines, -78 in the shell.

Kept deliberately: the 6px activation distance, data-no-drag on the close
button, and releaseTarget resolving the drop from release coordinates. Those
are the actual bug fix and the thing that made the drop reliable in CI.

Wiring detail: switched onDragOver to onDragMove. dragover only fires when
dnd-kit's resolved target CHANGES, which is exactly the signal CI proved
unreliable; dragmove fires on pointer movement, and the indicator is computed
from geometry anyway.

Tests: removed seven that asserted preview-mutation behaviour or were built
around stand-ins the preview caused - those scenarios can no longer occur.
Replaced with two that assert the invariant this design buys: a drag in flight
leaves membership, selection and route untouched, and a project deleted
mid-drag is handled normally with the drop still landing.

Test trap: mid-drag, BOTH the overlay and the placeholder carry
data-workspace-tab-active, so any active-tab assertion during a drag needs
:not([data-dnd-dragging]):not([data-dnd-placeholder]) or it hits strict mode.

